60.steps:
1. Configure interface to zone LAN, DMZ, and WLAN with different subnet classes;
2. Verify that under DHCP Server, LAN and WLAN ranges were added correctly;
3. Add DHCP range for DMZ;
4. Change expire time to 5 minutes;
5. Verify clients on each interface get leases successfully;
6. Do release/renew on each client, verify all clients get leases successfully;

73.steps:
1. configure dynamic DHCP entry;
2. Create two DHCP clients 1 and 2 for LAN, using CDRouter;
3. Change the request IP for client 1 to be out of DHCP range but still in the same subnet;
4. Do DHCP renew for client 1;
5. The renew should be failed;
6. Change the request IP for client 2 to be out of DHCP range and not in the same subnet;
7. Do DHCP renew for client 2;
8. The renew should be failed too

66.steps:
1. Configure DHCP Entry with address IP1 with a short lease time of 2 mins;
2. Configure a client to get the lease with IP1;
3. Disconnect the client as soon as the lease is obtained;
4. Now configure another client in the network;
5. IP1 must be leased to the new client after the 2 mins lease time
NOTE:in diag.html,you should configure as below
1. set "Time interval of DHCP lease database to be refreshed" to 60 Seconds
2. enable "Aggressively recycle expired DHCP leases in advance"

76.steps:
1. Load new firmware and reboot from factory default;
2. Configure SonicWALL through setup wizard, accept default settings as much as possible;
3. Once setup finished, go to Network > DHCP Server page, check if default WLAN DHCP range is available; by default, it should be from 172.16.31.2 to 172.16.31.254;
4. Check if wireless DHCP client can get WLAN DHCP lease

